# F3 examples

Library version `0.1.0`. Wire version 0.1. These cells use the committed `test/fixtures/small.f3` fixture and the public API. Row decoding needs the native NIF. On the default build, `F3.read/2` and `F3.stream/2` return `:native_unavailable` and do not read the payload.

The fixture has three rows and one row group. The fields are `trade_id` (`int64`), `symbol` (`utf8`), and `price` (`float64`). None of them are nullable.

## Section

## Open, inspect, and close

```elixir
{:ok, file} = F3.open("test/fixtures/small.f3")
{:ok, schema} = F3.schema(file, max_metadata_bytes: 1_048_576)
["trade_id", "symbol", "price"] = Enum.map(schema.fields, & &1.name)
{:ok, text} = F3.inspect(file, detail: false, format: :text)
true = text =~ "schema: trade_id int64, symbol utf8, price float64"
{:ok, meta} = F3.metadata(file)
{0, 1, 1} = {meta.major_version, meta.minor_version, length(meta.row_groups)}
{:ok, closed} = F3.close(file)
true = closed.closed
```

`F3.read/2` accepts `:columns`, `:row_groups`, `:batch_size` (default 8192), `:wasm` (`:off` or `:sandbox`), `:extensions`, and `:wasm_module_bytes`. A missing file, a closed handle, and a bad option return `%F3.Error{}`. They do not raise.

```elixir
{:ok, file} = F3.open("test/fixtures/small.f3")
{:error, read_error} = F3.read(file, columns: ["symbol"], batch_size: 2, wasm: :off)
:native_unavailable = read_error.category
{:error, stream_error} = F3.stream(file, row_groups: [0])
"native decoder is not loaded" = stream_error.message
{:error, missing} = F3.open("missing-file.f3")
:not_found = missing.category
:ok = F3.close(file) |> elem(0)
```

## A memory source

`F3.open/2` with `source: {:memory, binary}` does not open `path`. `pread/3` returns at most `length` bytes. A start at or past the end is an empty binary.

```elixir
{:ok, file} = F3.open("unused", source: {:memory, <<1, 2, 3, 4>>})
{:ok, state} = F3.IO.Memory.open(<<1, 2, 3, 4>>)
{:ok, 4} = F3.IO.Memory.size(state)
{:ok, <<2, 3>>} = F3.IO.Memory.pread(state, 1, 2)
{:ok, <<>>} = F3.IO.Memory.pread(state, 4, 2)
{:ok, closed} = F3.IO.Memory.close(state)
{:error, error} = F3.IO.Memory.size(closed)
:closed = error.category
:memory = file.origin
```

## Columns and one batch

A column is an Elixir binary of little-endian values. `F3.Batch.to_rows/1` is the small-result conversion. A large file should keep the columns.

```elixir
{:ok, ids} = F3.Column.from_native(:i64, 2, <<1::little-64, 2::little-64>>, nil)
2 = F3.Column.value(ids, 1)
true = F3.Column.matches?(ids, :integer)
sliced = F3.Column.slice(ids, 1, 1)
2 = F3.Column.value(sliced, 0)
field = %{name: "id", type: {:int, 64, true}, nullable: false}
batch = %F3.Batch{
  columns: %{"id" => ids},
  num_rows: 2,
  schema: %F3.Schema{fields: [field]}
}
{:ok, [%{"id" => 1}, %{"id" => 2}]} = F3.Batch.to_rows(batch)
"int64" = F3.Schema.type_label(field.type)
```

## Checksums and the wire version

Chunk checksums use XXH64 with seed 0. A `nil` checksum means the footer stored none, which is `:ok`.

```elixir
15154266338359012955 = F3.Checksum.xxh64("a")
15154266338359012955 = F3.Checksum.xxh64("a", 0)
:ok = F3.Checksum.verify("a", nil)
{:error, mismatch} = F3.Checksum.verify("a", 1)
:checksum = mismatch.category
true = F3.Format.compatible?(0, 1)
false = F3.Format.compatible?(0, 2)
32 = F3.Format.postscript_size()
"F3" = F3.Format.magic()
```

## An extension callback

An extension is an Elixir module. The file does not name it. The caller registers the module and passes that pid as `extensions:`. An extension error does not fall through into Wasm.

```elixir
defmodule F3.Examples.TradeCount do
  @behaviour F3.Extension

  @impl true
  def decode(_bytes, _metadata, :i64) do
    F3.Column.from_native(:i64, 1, <<9::little-64>>, nil)
  end

  def decode(_bytes, _metadata, _type) do
    {:error, F3.Error.unsupported_encoding(:decode, "only int64")}
  end
end

key = %{
  encoding: :custom_wasm,
  version: %{major: 1, minor: 0, patch: 0},
  compression: :uncompressed
}

{:ok, column} = F3.Examples.TradeCount.decode(<<1>>, Map.put(key, :wasm_id, nil), :i64)
9 = F3.Column.value(column, 0)
{:ok, pid} = F3.Registry.start_link(capacity: 1)
:ok = F3.Registry.register(pid, key, F3.Examples.TradeCount)
{:ok, F3.Examples.TradeCount} = F3.Registry.lookup(pid, Map.put(key, :wasm_id, 0))
:ok = F3.Registry.unregister(pid, key)
:error = F3.Registry.lookup(nil, key)
```

## Writer options, without a native helper

A missing schema, an unknown option, and an IOUnit above 64 MiB fail before any file is created. On the default build, a valid schema returns `:not_implemented` and also creates no file. This cell stays on the checks that are the same in both builds.

```elixir
{:error, missing_schema} = F3.Writer.open("unused.f3", [])
"schema is required" = missing_schema.message

{:error, unknown} =
  F3.Writer.open("unused.f3", schema: [id: :int64], source: :remote)

"unknown option source" = unknown.message

{:error, limited} =
  F3.Writer.open("unused.f3",
    schema: [price: {:float64, null: true}],
    iounit_bytes: 64 * 1024 * 1024 + 1
  )

:resource_limit = limited.category
{:error, closed} = F3.Writer.close(:nope)
:not_implemented = closed.category
```

## HTTP options that fail before a request

Redirects are refused. A partial signing key set is `:invalid_argument`. The secret is not stored on the error.

```elixir
{:error, url_error} = F3.open("unused", source: {:http, "ftp://example.test/trades.f3"})
"http url must be http or https" = url_error.message

{:error, keys} =
  F3.IO.HTTP.open("http://example.test/trades.f3", bucket: "trades", timeout_ms: 1_000)

"signed request needs endpoint, bucket, key, region, access_key, and secret_key" =
  keys.message
```

## One logical field

`F3.Logical` walks the schema in footer order. A primitive `int64` field consumes physical column 0.

```elixir
field = %{name: "id", type: {:int, 64, true}, nullable: false}
tree = %{id: :struct, children: [%{id: :flat, children: []}]}
true = F3.Logical.matches?(tree, [field])
{:ok, [{0, :i64}]} = F3.Logical.needed([field], ["id"])
{:ok, physical} = F3.Column.from_native(:i64, 1, <<5::little-64>>, nil)
{:ok, %{"id" => column}} = F3.Logical.assemble([field], ["id"], %{0 => physical})
5 = F3.Column.value(column, 0)
%{major: 0, minor: 21, patch: 0} = F3.Dispatch.cascade_version()
true = F3.Dispatch.cascade_native?(%{major: 0, minor: 21, patch: 0})
```
